{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 40,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover Jehovah answered Job, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall he that cavilleth contend with the Almighty?\nHe that argueth with God, let him answer it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered Jehovah, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I am of small account; what shall I answer thee?\nI lay my hand upon my mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Once have I spoken, and I will not answer;\nYea, twice, but I will proceed no further.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jehovah answered Job out of the whirlwind, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gird up thy loins now like a man:\nI will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou even annul my judgment?\nWilt thou condemn me, that thou mayest be justified?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or hast thou an arm like God?\nAnd canst thou thunder with a voice like him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deck thyself now with excellency and dignity;\nAnd array thyself with honor and majesty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pour forth the overflowings of thine anger;\nAnd look upon every one that is proud, and abase him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look on every one that is proud, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bring him low;\nAnd tread down the wicked where they stand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hide them in the dust together;\nBind their faces in the hidden ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will I also confess of thee\nThat thine own right hand can save thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold now, behemoth, which I made as well as thee;\nHe eateth grass as an ox.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo now, his strength is in his loins,\nAnd his force is in the muscles of his belly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He moveth his tail like a cedar:\nThe sinews of his thighs are knit together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His bones are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tubes of brass;\nHis limbs are like bars of iron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is the chief of the ways of God:\nHe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "only",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that made him giveth him his sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely the mountains bring him forth food,\nWhere all the beasts of the field do play.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He lieth under the lotus-trees,\nIn the covert of the reed, and the fen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lotus-trees cover him with their shade;\nThe willows of the brook compass him about.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, if a river overflow, he trembleth not;\nHe is confident, though a Jordan swell even to his mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.40.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall any take him when he is on the watch,\nOr pierce through his nose with a snare?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
